{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":18381,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,7]],"date-time":"2026-10-07T17:28:39Z","timestamp":1791394119051,"version":"4.3.3"},"reference-count":4,"publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2004,1,1]],"date-time":"2004-01-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1072915200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/ieeexplore.ieee.org\/Xplorehelp\/downloads\/license-information\/IEEE.html"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["IEEE Secur. Privacy Mag."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2004,1]]},"DOI":"10.1109\/msecp.2004.1264852","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2004,2,24]],"date-time":"2004-02-24T21:01:05Z","timestamp":1077656465000},"page":"38-47","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":256,"title":["Secret-ballot receipts: true voter-verifiable elections"],"prefix":"10.1109","volume":"2","author":[{"given":"D.","family":"Chaum","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"263","reference":[{"key":"refs1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1145\/358549.358563"},{"key":"refs2","first-page":"339","article-title":"Making Mix Nets Robust for Electronic Voting by Randomized Partial Checking","volume-title":"Proc. Usenix Security 2002","author":"Jakobsson","year":"2002"},{"key":"ref1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/BFb0053419"},{"key":"ref2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/j.1538-7305.1949.tb00928.x"}],"container-title":["IEEE Security &amp; Privacy Magazine"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx5\/8013\/28290\/01264852.pdf?arnumber=1264852","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,16]],"date-time":"2025-03-16T04:11:41Z","timestamp":1742098301000},"score":23.565086,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/ieeexplore.ieee.org\/document\/1264852\/"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2004,1]]},"references-count":4,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2004,1]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/msecp.2004.1264852","ISSN":["1540-7993"],"issn-type":[{"value":"1540-7993","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2004,1]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,3]],"date-time":"2026-09-03T05:17:32Z","timestamp":1788412652311,"version":"build-2803163510"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,1]],"date-time":"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1767225600000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-nc\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>This paper specifies a Layer-1 blockchain protocol whose monetary issuance is mechanically indexed to the network's verifiable operating cost plus a small, bounded margin. New tokens are minted only to the extent required to cover attested energy, compute, and infrastructure expenditure incurred in processing and finalizing blocks, and to fund a stability buffer. The design objective is a cryptoasset whose issuance adjusts to verified operating cost and prevailing token value, limiting cumulative dilution and dampening price volatility over time without reliance on fiat reserves. This revision incorporates a significant development in market infrastructure: the emergence of independent GPU rental-rate benchmarks and exchange-listed compute derivatives, which supply the protocol with regulated, market-settled reference rates for its cost oracle and permit hedging of the protocol's cost base. We present the issuance rule, admissible cost basis, attestation architecture, oracle design, fee and buffer mechanics, consensus model, threat model, governance, and institutional use cases for real-world-asset (RWA) tokenization and settlement.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.7390378","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,3]],"date-time":"2026-09-03T04:52:33Z","timestamp":1788411153000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Cost-Indexed Crypto: A Framework for Volatility-Dampening Monetary Issuance Through Verifiable Operating Costs and Exchange-Settled Compute Benchmarks"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"given":"Matthew","family":"Schneider","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Robert","family":"Orozco","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"78","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,3]],"date-time":"2026-09-03T04:52:33Z","timestamp":1788411153000},"score":22.28192,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=7390378"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.7390378","published":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,7]],"date-time":"2026-03-07T17:31:54Z","timestamp":1772904714244,"version":"3.50.1"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>Agentic AI systems capable of goal-directed planning, tool-use, and autonomous execution are being adopted in high-stakes financial workflows where error costs are non-linear and correlated failures can amplify systemic risk. Current governance approaches (model risk management, operational resilience, and AI management systems) provide essential controls but do not yet provide a finance-grade assurance pattern for multi-agent autonomy: they often lack (i) machine-verifiable policy gating for agentic actions, (ii) evidence packet standards that bind intent, tool calls, and outcomes, (iii) attestation-linked deployment controls, and (iv) an operational metric that treats model monoculture and correlated agent behavior as a first-class risk. This paper proposes a Finance-Grade Verifiable Governance Architecture (FG-VGA): a layered control system combining policy-as-code, auditable evidence packets, remote attestation, systemic-risk coupling metrics, and compute\/sustainability accounting. The architecture decomposes safety into four auditable \"currencies\" (probabilistic safety, energy and compute safety, epistemic safety, and social and environmental safety) and reassembles them into a governance pipeline aligned with supervisory expectations (model risk management, operational resilience). This paper operationalizes monoculture risk through a Heterogeneity Score (H S)that enforces cross-vendor\/model diversification as an auditable authorization gate, directly addressing systemic risk amplification concerns raised by ESRB, FSB, and national regulators (FINMA). The paper includes operational blueprints, resource estimates, success metrics, a synthetic case study, and red-team scenarios to support implementation. Finally, an additive functional (variational) formulation is provided that generalizes scalar gates to computable functionals (via finite probe sets and parameterized policies), enabling sensitivity analysis and automated calibration without altering the discrete governance mechanics.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.6306980","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,7]],"date-time":"2026-03-07T01:06:56Z","timestamp":1772845616000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Finance-Grade Assurance for Agentic AI: Verifiable Governance, Systemic Risk Mitigation, and Sustainability\/Compute Accounting Architecture for Banks, Insurers, and Major Financial Services Providers"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"given":"Georgios","family":"Fradelos","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"78","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,7]],"date-time":"2026-03-07T01:06:56Z","timestamp":1772845616000},"score":21.361345,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=6306980"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.6306980","published":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,2]],"date-time":"2026-10-02T16:56:19Z","timestamp":1790960179896,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":39,"publisher":"IEEE","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,2]],"date-time":"2025-06-02T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1748822400000},"content-version":"stm-asf","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.15223\/policy-029"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,2]],"date-time":"2025-06-02T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1748822400000},"content-version":"stm-asf","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.15223\/policy-037"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,2]]},"DOI":"10.1109\/icbc64466.2025.11114627","type":"proceedings-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,8,14]],"date-time":"2025-08-14T18:34:30Z","timestamp":1755196470000},"page":"1-9","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":6,"title":["Trusted Compute Units: A Framework for Chained Verifiable Computations"],"prefix":"10.1109","author":[{"given":"Fernando","family":"Castillo","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Technische Universit&#x00E4;t Berlin,Information Systems Engineering,Berlin,Germany"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jonathan","family":"Heiss","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Technische Universit&#x00E4;t Berlin,Information Systems Engineering,Berlin,Germany"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Sebastian","family":"Werner","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Technische Univers